# LIVE REGRESSION FIXTURE for `t0697`/`t0709` — a `Vector[Box[Trait]]` built
# with `Box.new` + `push` and returned from a helper. It used to segfault
# (rc 139 on both backends, ASan `stack-buffer-overflow` in
# `__interceptor_memcpy`) because the trait-object pack never ran at a builtin
# consuming position: no destination type reached the pack AT ALL — a builtin
# collection method leaves `method_param_types` empty, so the pack's
# `callee_param_type` was `None` and it returned early without deciding
# anything. `Box[Robot]` was handed straight to `Vector__Box__Speaker__push`
# and the
# runtime memcpy'd 16 bytes of `{data, vtable}` out of an 8-byte `void*` slot.
#
# ⚠ DISCRIMINATED FROM ITS SIBLING BY FORMATION SPELLING — do not merge them.
# The same program written with the CTOR CALL and a CONTAINER LITERAL --
# `Box(Robot(...))` + `Vector[Box[Speaker]] v = [b]` -- failed DIFFERENTLY:
# rc 0 printing the EMPTY STRING on both lanes, ASan `heap-use-after-free` in
# `gorget_string_clone_to_owned`.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE NAMED-LOCAL SPELLING. `v.push(^b)` moves an owning named local
# into the collection; its sibling
# `known_gaps/vec_box_trait_pushed_no_helper.gg` pushes a TEMP. The two took
# different paths to the same overflow and are both pinned.
#
# ⚠ The payload is heap-forced through `mk`. A literal would not reallocate
# and would hide the defect.
#
# ⚠ It stays in `known_gaps/` deliberately: moving the file registers a
# non-MATCH against `RUNTIME_DIFF_NONMATCH_CEILING`, and Core #9 ⊕ forbids
# raising that ceiling for own inflow. The self-host lane has no analogue of
# the GIR-level pack at consuming positions and still crashes here.
#
# INTENDED: prints `R2` on both backends.
from std.collections import Box
trait Speaker:
    String speak(self)
struct Robot:
    String id
equip Robot with Speaker:
    String speak(self):
        return self.id

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

Vector[Box[Speaker]] make():
    Box[Robot] b = Box.new(Robot(mk("R", "2")))
    Vector[Box[Speaker]] v = []
    v.push(^b)
    return v

void main():
    Vector[Box[Speaker]] v = make()
    print(v.get(0).unwrap().speak())
